Hi,

> I just got AlphaServer DS10 working (replaced bad PSU capacitors, 3.3V rail was only 2.7V).
> 
> SRM supports booting from 3X-DEGXA-T* (Broadcom 570x), but NetBSD can't be installed from it.
> 
> Could you add bge driver to the installer kernel?
> 
> I can of course use the network ports on the motherboard, they are detected fine, but would like the gigabit speed.

Apologies - this was on my list, but I forgot until now.   I've added bge
to the INSTALL config, so the next autobuilds will have it.

Would you like it for the 11.0 release as well?  There might be just time to
get it in.

Regards,

Julian

-- 


